[{"sha":"f11e04e317d8188b249dd5cc6ca20cb72661443c","node_id":"C_kwDOANo_SNoAKGYxMWUwNGUzMTdkODE4OGIyNDlkZDVjYzZjYTIwY2I3MjY2MTQ0M2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Vas Crabb","email":"vas@vastheman.com","date":"2026-09-23T22:05:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"Vas Crabb","email":"vas@vastheman.com","date":"2026-09-23T22:19:02Z"},"message":"Cleaned up some APIs:\n\nGot rid of driver_start and driver_reset.  These are leftovers from the\npre-device world where driver_start/driver_reset were for drivers/*.*\nand machine_start/machine/reset were for machine/*.*.  Having both of\nthem just makes things confusing, and there was a clear preference for\nthe \"machine\" variants.\n\nemu/distate.cpp: Got rid of some C string pointers in APIs, allow the\nlinker to coalesce out-of-line instantiations of state_add templates.\nTo follow up, .c_str() calls can be removed from calls to state_add in\nvarious CPU devices.\n\nmatsushita/jr200.cpp: Added some missing read side effects checks.\n\nmisc/policetr.cpp: Use machine configuration functions rather than crazy\nclass hierarchy to set speedup hack parameters.\n\nnamco/galaga.cpp, namco/xevious.cpp: Got the xevious_state and derived\nstuff out of galaga.cpp so the classes and files actually have a\ncorrespondence to each other.  Required copy/pasting a crystal value and\na planar graphics layout.","tree":{"sha":"8c017d7b31f7efb4922596d3aa6112a33e08e56e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mamedev/mame/git/trees/8c017d7b31f7efb4922596d3aa6112a33e08e56e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mamedev/mame/git/commits/f11e04e317d8188b249dd5cc6ca20cb72661443c","comment_count":1,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mamedev/mame/commits/f11e04e317d8188b249dd5cc6ca20cb72661443c","html_url":"https://github.com/mamedev/mame/commit/f11e04e317d8188b249dd5cc6ca20cb72661443c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mamedev/mame/commits/f11e04e317